# pilot-wp CLI — configuration (everything here is OPTIONAL).
#
# Copy to "config.env" next to pilot-wp-common.sh and `chmod 600`. Every value can
# also be supplied as an environment variable, which takes precedence over this
# file. The authoritative defaults live in
# pilot-wp-common.sh and the scripts, and are documented one-per-row in TECHNICAL.md
# ("Variables"); this file only surfaces the settings you might want to change, with
# the default shown after `=`. Uncomment a line to override it.
#
# A plain free-to-air install needs nothing in this file — just:
#     ./pilot-wp-login        # create the cookie jar (paste a browser Copy-as-cURL)
#     ./pilot-wp-m3u out.m3u  # generate the playlist
# Check a setup any time with:  ./pilot-wp-status

# =============================================================================
# QUICK START — the settings most people touch
# =============================================================================

# Authentication needs nothing here: the cookie jar (cookies.txt) is the auth
# artifact — create/refresh it with `./pilot-wp-login`.

# DRM playback. OFF by default: protected channels (e.g. TVN) show an info slate.
# Set to 1 AND provide an L3 Widevine device file (drop a *.wvd into widevine/, or
# set PILOT_WP_WVD) to decrypt and play them. See README.md (setup) and TECHNICAL.md "DRM playback".
#PILOT_WP_DRM_ENABLE=0

# =============================================================================
# ADVANCED — rarely needed. Uncomment to override the default shown.
# Full descriptions: TECHNICAL.md "Variables".
# =============================================================================

# --- Paths / identity --------------------------------------------------------
#PILOT_WP_HOME=                # dir holding the jar/lock/cache (default: the scripts dir)
#PILOT_WP_COOKIES=$PILOT_WP_HOME/cookies.txt
#PILOT_WP_LOCKFILE=$PILOT_WP_HOME/.lock
#DEVICE_TYPE=android_tv        # API device class

# --- Retry / multiroom (concurrent-stream) limit -----------------------------
#PILOT_WP_RETRIES=3            # per-tune (auth + open) attempts before giving up
#PILOT_WP_LIMIT_RETRIES=3      # open retries on the concurrent-stream limit
#PILOT_WP_LIMIT_DELAY=2        # seconds between those retries

# --- M3U DRM tag scan --------------------------------------------------------
# pilot-wp-m3u probes channels (incrementally, with a cache) to add a "DRM" tag to
# protected ones. Set 0 to skip probing entirely (no DRM tag).
#PILOT_WP_M3U_DRM_SCAN=1
#PILOT_WP_M3U_CACHE_TTL_DAYS=7 # re-probe a cached channel once older than this (max 7)
# (force a full re-probe once with: ./pilot-wp-m3u --rescan OUTPUT_PATH)
#PILOT_WP_M3U_CACHE=$PILOT_WP_HOME/.m3u-drm-cache.tsv
#PILOT_WP_DRM_VERIFY_TIMEOUT=8 # seconds for the manifest check of a channel that advertises DRM

# --- Session keepalive (pilot-wp-ping; for an idle box on cron) --------------
#PILOT_WP_PING_TIMEOUT=15      # seconds for the single probe request
#PILOT_WP_PING_LOG=            # if set, append one outcome line per run

# --- DRM-only settings (PILOT_WP_DRM_ENABLE=1) --------------------------------
#PILOT_WP_WVD=                 # path to an L3 .wvd (default: first *.wvd in widevine/)
#PILOT_WP_DRM_KEY_LOG=         # append pilot-wp-getkeys stderr here (debug)

# --- DASH pipeline (DRM channels, and free-to-air while PILOT_WP_FTA_DASH=1) ---
# These apply to every channel played through pilot-wp-dashlive, clear or encrypted.
#PILOT_WP_PYTHON=              # runs dashlive (stdlib); DRM also needs pywidevine (default: .drmvenv, else python3)
#PILOT_WP_REFRESH_INTERVAL=100   # proactive session refresh (s) for token-gated channels
# ffmpeg for the DASH restream (+ decrypt). -copyts is required: it preserves A/V
# sync on number-based channels. Don't add HLS/network flags here.
#PILOT_WP_DASH_FFMPEG_FLAGS=-loglevel fatal -copyts
# Extra pilot-wp-dashlive args as one string. Common ones:
#   --parallel N        concurrent connections per video track (default 3)
#   --prebuffer N       ready segments delivered up front (default 20; capped to
#                       the stream's time-shift window)
#   --max-video-bw BITS cap the video rendition, e.g. 4000000 (default: highest)
#   --behind N          segments kept behind the live edge (default 2)
#   --verbose           log per-segment fetch timing (debug)
#PILOT_WP_DASHLIVE_ARGS=   # e.g. "--prebuffer 15 --max-video-bw 4000000"

# --- Free-to-air playback / tracing ------------------------------------------
#PILOT_WP_FTA_DASH=1           # FTA via DASH + pilot-wp-dashlive; 0 = HLS (the flags below)
#PILOT_WP_FTA_DASH_CODEC=avc1  # preferred FTA DASH video codec; empty = first set (may be HEVC)
# ffmpeg flags for the HLS path (FTA_DASH=0, or no DASH URL / no python). Keep the
# large analysis window: it lets ffmpeg find Pilot WP's separate audio renditions
# (incl. the offset audio-description track). Drop -live_start_index -1 if a flaky
# channel underruns (slower tune, bigger cushion behind the live edge).
#PILOT_WP_HLS_FFMPEG_FLAGS=-loglevel fatal -probesize 15M -analyzeduration 6000000 -live_start_index -1 -reconnect 1 -reconnect_at_eof 1 -reconnect_streamed 1 -reconnect_delay_max 5
#PILOT_WP_TRACE=0              # 1 = emit debug lines to stderr (captured in the tvheadend log)
#PILOT_WP_RELEASE_LOG=         # if set, the detached slot-releaser appends its actions here

# --- Slate (shown for DRM-unavailable / over-limit / auth-fail) --------------
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_LOGO=           # local image used as the logo on every slate, instead of the channel logo
# Messages use \n for line breaks (channel name is added automatically when no logo):
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_TEXT_DRM=
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_TEXT_LIMIT=
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_TEXT_AUTH=
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_BG=0x101820    # background colour
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_SIZE=1280x720  # slate resolution
# Text font; if the file is missing, the slate is drawn without any text.
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_FONT=/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_FONTSIZE=32    # message text size
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_TITLE_FONTSIZE=56  # channel-name title size (when no logo)
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_TOP=60         # top margin above the logo/title
#PILOT_WP_SLATE_GAP=90         # space between the logo/title band and the message
